  "step_3": "The decision reason requires: (1) identifying small-probability outcomes (here, 1% in B), (2) increasing their probability weight by 10 percentage points (to 11%), and (3) computing a weighted sum of outcomes based on these adjusted probabilities to determine preference. The individual in the report does not mention adjusting the 1% probability, nor does the individual refer to any weighting rule or calculation of a weighted sum. Instead, the individual only notes that B offers a chance to earn more and that the 1% risk of earning nothing is 'extremely low'. This reflects a risk perception or intuitive assessment, not the application of the specific decision reason. Therefore, while the individual arrives at the same choice (B), the reasoning process does not involve the stated rule of increasing small-probability weights. The decision reason was not used in the deliberation process as described.",
